          "kind": "text",
          "text": "\"My blood pressure has been dipping under 100, sometimes down into the 90s, when I measure it at home... should I cut back on my medication?\" I've been getting this question more often lately. It's actually quite common for blood pressure to drop even when your weight and daily habits haven't changed — seasonal shifts (blood vessels tend to widen more easily in summer, which can lower blood pressure) and simply how you're feeling that day can both move the number."
