    "en": {
      "category": "A message from the director",
      "title": "In a world where interest rates are back, we are building this clinic with full commitment",
      "excerpt": "“Your loan has been approved” — when the bank told me this, before any relief, I felt myself sit up straighter. As times change in a big way, here is the commitment I have made as director.",
      "body": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "“Will this clinic really last for years to come?” Some of you may feel this way about a newly opening clinic. And for those of you thinking about working with us, there may be a worry about whether it is safe to entrust your future to this workplace. Those feelings are completely natural."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Recently, the bank informed us that our loan for opening the clinic had been approved. To be honest, what I felt at that moment was not so much relief as a sense of resolve: this is really happening."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "So in this post, I'd like to explain how Japan's economy is changing right now, and what kind of clinic we are aiming to be in the middle of it. The short version: **an era with interest rates is one in which organizations that just carry on “somehow” are weeded out, and only those that truly deliver value remain. That is exactly why we are building this clinic with full commitment to contributing to local healthcare.**"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "## A major change happening in Japan's economy"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "### The era of “zero interest rates” has ended"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "For a long time, Japan was in a state known as “zero interest rates”. You could borrow money from a bank and pay almost no interest."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The benchmark for this is the **policy interest rate** set by the Bank of Japan. It is, in a sense, the source of all interest rates in Japan: when it rises, the rates banks charge on loans and the interest paid on deposits rise as well."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "### Into a “world with interest rates”"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The Bank of Japan, aiming for an economy in which prices rise steadily at around 2%, is now raising the policy rate step by step. Borrow money, and you pay proper interest on it. Japan is returning to this normal **“world with interest rates”**."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "While reviewing the terms of our loan, I calculated again and again how much changes in interest rates would affect our repayments. This is by no means someone else's problem — it applies to clinics too."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "## An era with interest rates is an era that tests true commitment"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "### “Somehow” no longer works"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "When interest costs almost nothing, organizations can keep going even if they are a little inefficient. But once borrowed money carries interest, things change."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Organizations that cannot create more value than the money they spend will gradually struggle to continue. In other words, I believe a tough but healthy era has begun, in which **only organizations that truly deliver value remain**."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "### Medical institutions are no exception"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Healthcare is important work that protects the health of the community. That is exactly why “it's always been here” or “it just keeps going” will not be enough to keep earning the community's trust in the years ahead. To remain a clinic that patients and staff keep choosing, I believe daily effort is essential."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "## Three things we are seriously investing in"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "### 1. The quality of care for patients"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "We are putting in place CT, gastroscopy and abdominal ultrasound so that worrying symptoms can be checked the same day. We have also worked from the building's design stage to help everyone visit with peace of mind, for example by separating the flow for patients with a fever from other patients ([our post on separating patients with a fever](/blog/kansen-dousen-bunri))."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "### 2. Giving back to the staff we work with"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Good care only comes from a good team. We are seriously committed to creating a comfortable work environment and fair treatment that properly rewards hard work, so that our staff can work with pride for a long time."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "### 3. Systems that reduce waiting and hassle"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "We are introducing systems such as online booking and our website's guide chatbot, Kibanavi, to reduce waiting times and hassle for patients. By letting systems handle what they can, we want to give our staff more time to spend with patients."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "## To the community, and to our future colleagues"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "To everyone in the community: we are taking every step of our preparations seriously as we head toward opening in October 2027. We will build a clinic that makes you feel, “I'm glad I came here.”"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "And to those who will work with us: we are building a new team from scratch. Won't you join us in creating a workplace where hard work is properly rewarded ([our careers page](/careers))?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Even as times change, one promise stays the same: we will keep facing the health of our community with full commitment. Please keep watching over us until we open."
        }
      ]
    }
